<title>ITALY: Italy air traffic control staff plan hunger strike.</title>
<headline>Italy air traffic control staff plan hunger strike.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air traffic control staff at Rome's Fiumicino airport said on Monday they were planning to go on hunger strike from June 6 to protest against what they see as reduced safety standards.</p>
<p>The small independent trade union Sulta said in a statement that an end to night technical surveillance of radar and other equipment from the start of June had put flight safety at risk.</p>
<p>The union said workers wanted authorisation to continue guaranteeing a night-time service, and would fund it out of their own pockets and in their own time.</p>
<p>The hunger strike will begin in front of a pharmacy in the international departures lounge, it said.</p>
